# Agent Wallet Bench

Coding agents set up crypto wallets and use them on their own. Each square is one agent with one wallet; its link opens the exact recorded run shown in that square.

Each square shows one latest matching attempt across all sets, keeping its nine criterion positions in order. A newer failed install stays visible even when an older wallet attempt passed. Unclear, not recorded, not run and not applicable are distinct from a failed check. Money tests use five checks and four not-applicable positions. Previous runs and repeated-set comparisons remain on the pair's page. Model, agent, wallet and protocol filters narrow the same records in every representation.
<%= for {key, selected} <- @matrix.filters, selected != "", option <- @matrix.options[key], option.id == selected do %>
- <%= key %> filter: <%= line(option.label) %><% end %>
<%= for grid <- @matrix.grids do %>
## <%= grid_title(grid.grid) %>

<%= grid.tested %> of <%= grid.total %> squares have results; <%= grid.never_run %> never run.

<%= grid_table(@matrix, grid) %>
<% end %>
[How the bench works](/wallet-bench/how-it-works): the checks, what each result means, and how Techtree runs each test.
<%= trailer() %>
